<title>FRANCE: French govt declines comment on GEC report.</title>
<headline>French govt declines comment on GEC report.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>The French finance ministry declined comment on newspaper reports on Wednesday that Britain's GEC Plc had made a bid for defence electronics group Thomson-CSF.</p>
<p>Daily newspapers La Tribune and Le Figaro both said GEC had submitted a bid by the deadline fixed last Friday, rivalling French companies Lagardere and Alcatel Alsthom.</p>
<p>A finance ministry spokeswoman said she had no comment on the reports.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 42 21 53 81</p>
